# The build context for infra/Dockerfile.
#
# This file lives at the repository root rather than beside the Dockerfile because
# that is the only location every builder honours. BuildKit would also read
# `infra/Dockerfile.dockerignore`, but `az acr build` — which is how deploy.sh
# builds the image, with no local Docker daemon — would not, and a context
# containing node_modules is a slow upload and a confusing cache. See ADR-033.
#
# Everything below is either rebuilt inside the image or has no business in it.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Rebuilt by `pnpm build` in the build stage. Copying a host build in would ship
# whatever happened to be on someone's laptop.
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
coverage
**/coverage

# Secrets. `.env.example` is deliberately not excluded — it documents the
# variables and contains no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git
.github
.claude
docs
infra
README.md

.DS_Store
*.log
